rk is within almost within the margin of error four point race, but straight up between him as a Republican and the Democrat. Kathy Honko, and then there's this odd, you know, you don't know what's going to happen factor that Andrew Cuomo might run as an independent. That's that would make things interesting. What does it mean for New York? It means that I actually truly for the first time believe that New York might be ready to say enough is enough and elect a Republican governor to fix things and change things, which it desperately needs. If it wants to be competitive and stop bleeding out all of the residents that have, I mean, the exodus is just like California, just like New Jersey, just like Illinois, And people said they've had enough and they're just leaving, they're packing their bags, selling their homes, and they're moving to states like Texas and Tennessee and the Carolinas and Florida is inundated, home prices in Florida have never been like they are today. In large park, there's little demand, there's a little inventory on the market because there's such a high demand. Um, anyway, Kathleen Hochl is now put forward a record, you know, deficit creating budget announcing a green agenda for New York. Um, and saying that by, I think the year's 20, 27, you know, we're going to have to build skyscrapers with toothpicks based on there'll be no use of any fossil fuels at all in the building of anything. Well, what if you need a generator and we're going to get that generator from anyway, listen,",
